{
  "id": "KP33Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Shoulder arthroscopy",
  "description": "A surgical shoulder repair is an outpatient procedure where your surgeon repairs damaged shoulder structures using arthroscopic (minimally invasive) or open surgical techniques. Shoulder injuries like rotator cuff tears, labral tears, or impingement can cause pain and loss of function. Your surgeon will assess your shoulder and perform the necessary repairs. The procedure takes 1-2 hours, and you may go home the same day or stay overnight. You'll typically wear a sling and avoid strenuous activities for 4-6 weeks while you heal. Physical therapy is essential and begins soon after surgery, progressing gradually from gentle motion to strengthening exercises. You'll have specific restrictions during healing. Your surgeon may perform arthroscopic repair through small incisions or use larger open incisions depending on your injury severity. This type of procedure can be performed various ways, including arthroscopic decompression/debridement and arthroscopic repair, and the cost may vary depending on the specific approach or service provided.",
